
## Running Tests

This package includes the mysql-test framework (`mysql-test/`) for extension authors to write and run tests.

@TEST_NOTE@

### Running Extension Tests

When developing an extension, specify your test suite directory and VEB location:

```bash
cd mysql-test

# Run all tests in your extension's test suite
./mysql-test-run.pl --suite=/path/to/your/extension/tests \
                    --veb-source-dir=/path/to/your/extension/build

# Run with parallel execution
./mysql-test-run.pl --suite=/path/to/your/extension/tests \
                    --veb-source-dir=/path/to/your/extension/build \
                    --parallel=auto

# Run a specific test (test name as positional argument)
./mysql-test-run.pl --suite=/path/to/your/extension/tests \
                    --veb-source-dir=/path/to/your/extension/build \
                    my_test

# Record test results (for creating .result files)
./mysql-test-run.pl --suite=/path/to/your/extension/tests \
                    --veb-source-dir=/path/to/your/extension/build \
                    --record
```

**Options:**
- `--suite` - Path to your test suite directory or specific test file
- `--veb-source-dir` - Path to directory containing your `.veb` files (can be specified multiple times)
- `--parallel=auto` - Run tests in parallel for faster execution
- `--record` - Update test result files

### Test Organization

Create your extension tests in:
- `mysql-test/suite/my_extension/` - Your test suite
- `mysql-test/suite/my_extension/t/` - Test files (.test)
- `mysql-test/suite/my_extension/r/` - Expected results (.result)

Example test file structure:
```
mysql-test/suite/my_extension/
├── t/
│   ├── basic.test
│   └── advanced.test
└── r/
    ├── basic.result
    └── advanced.result
```

See `mysql-test/README` for more information on writing tests.
